ta","data":[{"unit":1,"title":3,"area":112,"prev":114,"next":116,"titles":119,"firmware":54},{"id":2,"title":3,"aliases":4,"area":11,"order":12,"path":13,"context":14,"summary":18,"status":19,"firmware":20,"facts":25,"procedures":64,"parameters":87,"related":88,"body":92,"sources":93,"official_url":29,"controls":100},"mix.mute-solo","Mute and solo",[5,6,7,8,9,10],"mute","unmute","solo","mute track","solo track","mute shortcut","mix",20,"knowledge/manual/units/mix/mute-solo.md",{"modes":15,"screens":16},[11],[17],"M1","In mix mode, shift + a track key mutes or unmutes that track and holding track keys solos them; instrument or auxiliary + a track key is a quick mute, and CC9 mutes over MIDI.","current",{"min":21,"changed_in":22,"guide_version":23,"verified_on":24},"1.0.9",[],"1.1.15",null,[26,31,36,39,42,45,47,50,56,61],{"id":27,"text":28,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"shift-mute","In mix mode, `shift + Tn` mutes that track, or unmutes it if it is muted.","https://teenage.engineering/guides/op-xy/mix#levels-pans-and-sends","official",{"id":32,"text":33,"source":34,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":35},"arrange-mute","`shift + Tn` mutes and unmutes in arrange mode as well, in tutorial videos on OS 1.0.x.","docs/research/65-video-tutorials.md#217-arrange-patterns-scenes-songs-sound-link","community-verified",{"id":37,"text":38,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"leds","While `shift` is held in mix mode, unmuted tracks light up (white for instrument, red for auxiliary) and muted tracks stay dark.",{"id":40,"text":41,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"notes-not-audio","A mute acts on a track's notes, not on its audio; no new notes start, while sound that is already playing rings out.",{"id":43,"text":44,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"click","On the mix `M1` page, `click E4` mutes the selected track.",{"id":7,"text":46,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"Holding one track key, or several at once, in mix mode solos those tracks.",{"id":48,"text":49,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"shortcut","Holding `instrument` and pressing a track key mutes or unmutes that instrument track; `auxiliary` does the same for the auxiliary tracks.",{"id":51,"text":52,"source":53,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":54,"confidence":55},"midi","Over MIDI, CC9 on a track's channel sets its mute as a level rather than a toggle — 0 unmutes, any value from 1 to 127 mutes.","docs/research/90-device-probe.md#2026-09-26--session-1-results-owner-present-scratch-project-os-1133","1.1.33","verified",{"id":57,"text":58,"source":59,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":60},"grey-strip","On the mix page a muted strip's bar and lines are drawn grey (two videos, OS 1.0.x and 1.1.x).","docs/research/78-overnight-accuracy.md#log","community",{"id":62,"text":63,"source":59,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":60},"held-edit","Tutorial videos show that holding track keys in mix mode also lets one encoder turn edit all the held tracks together, see the levels-pans-sends unit.",[65,72,79],{"id":5,"goal":66,"preconditions":67,"steps":69,"result":24,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"Mute or unmute a track",[68],"mix mode",[70],{"keys":71,"note":24,"set":24},"shift + Tn",{"id":7,"goal":73,"preconditions":74,"steps":75,"result":24,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"Solo one or more tracks",[68],[76],{"keys":77,"note":78,"set":24},"hold Tn","hold more track keys at the same time to solo several",{"id":80,"goal":81,"preconditions":82,"steps":83,"result":24,"source":29,"firmware_min":24,"verified_on":24,"confidence":30},"quick-mute","Mute a track with the mode-key shortcut",[],[84],{"keys":85,"note":86,"set":24},"instrument/auxiliary + Tn","the guide lists this under mix mode; whether it works in other modes is not confirmed",[],[89,90,91],"mix.levels-pans-sends","mix.overview","arrange.overview","`shift` shows the mute state on the track keys and toggles it; holding track keys solos them; and\n`instrument` or `auxiliary` double as mute modifiers for their own group. A click on `E4` mutes the\nselected track in arrange mode too. Mutes stop notes rather than cutting audio, so tails finish\nnaturally.",[94,96,98,99],{"url":29,"kind":95},"guide",{"url":34,"kind":97},"research",{"url":53,"kind":97},{"url":59,"kind":97},[101,102,103,104,105,106,107,108,109,110,111],"key.shift","track.1","track.2","track.3","track.4","track.5","track.6","track.7","track.8","key.instrument","key.auxiliary",{"id":11,"title":113},"Mix",{"id":89,"title":115},"Levels, pans and sends",{"id":117,"title":118},"mix.eq","Master EQ",{"basics.key-notation":120,"basics.main-modes":121,"basics.modules":122,"basics.track-buttons":123,"basics.linked-tracks":124,"basics.patterns-scenes-songs":125,"basics.workflow":126,"basics.firmware-versions":127,"hardware.layout":128,"hardware.power-and-charging":129,"hardware.connectors":130,"hardware.specifications":131,"hardware.te-boot":132,"hardware.firmware-update":133,"hardware.factory-reset":134,"hardware.system-menu":135,"hardware.safety-and-care":136,"hardware.in-the-box":137,"sequencer.overview":138,"sequencer.step-entry":139,"sequencer.step-recording":140,"sequencer.live-recording":141,"sequencer.extend-notes":142,"sequencer.nudge":143,"sequencer.single-sound":144,"sequencer.rotate":145,"sequencer.copy-step":146,"sequencer.transpose-sequence":147,"sequencer.parameter-locks":148,"sequencer.clear-and-undo":149,"sequencer.step-components":150,"sequencer.step-component-reference":151,"sequencer.component-pulse":152,"sequencer.component-pulse-hold":153,"sequencer.component-multiply":154,"sequencer.component-velocity":155,"sequencer.component-ramp-up":156,"sequencer.component-ramp-down":157,"sequencer.component-random":158,"sequencer.component-portamento":159,"sequenc